- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used to carry the message out

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

The channel
-----------

There is no Bluetooth, no cable API and no QR camera in this app. The channel is a JSON file the person
carries themselves — on a cable, a USB stick, or by opening it on the other device. The spec's
"auto-selects the best channel" is therefore not built: there is one channel, and it is stated rather than
invented.

What is built: the chain of hand-offs, the hash that catches an edited body, and the refusal to claim
delivery.

What this app does not promise
------------------------------

A hand-off records that someone took the message. It does not record that it arrived. Those are different
claims and only the first is knowable here, so the app says "does not promise it arrived" at the moment of
every hand-off, and the received view calls itself a record of hand-offs rather than a delivery receipt.
